  "contracts": [
    "Whole ordinary C preview/connection/route-footprint algorithms reused; model/frame/Original wrappers are not counted.3 existing current C query bodies adopted unchanged.",
    "46FEF0 retains tool-specific preview effects, warnings, unchanged routing/painting children, credit and count scaling. Definition size uses earlier237-row Native DWORD/BYTE proof. Four venue constructors consume lastX/lastY, not ignored first coordinates.",
    "47EDA0 restores terrain and cleared bytes using actual0040F860 source,destination,count convention, then restores free image slots. Signed wrapped deltas/statuses,16 endpoint trials, strict best-count update and per-endpoint water-lift cost are retained.",
    "47CA50 sets actual BC9768 after Native bounds checks even for empty height; mode0 clears actual EED760 cells at Native8-byte footprint-table offsets. No extra size/cycle clamp.",
    "486A30 saves both genuine shore-query coordinates, computes real ferry distances/path, publishes count only then and caches doubled radius once. Orientation-specific trapezoid scanning and wrapped native integer arithmetic are retained.",
    "46FEF0 ferry linking keeps BYTE AA orientation overlay, signedWORD IDs, actual peer DWORD C4 and shared BCA310/BCA315/BC9800.486020 ignores caller PUSH value; the real BC9800 pointer is passed to its C API.",
    "486BF0 returns real999 for boundary rejection,0/1 otherwise; CF0 keeps signed quotient/remainder. Existing C query producer domain is ordinary valid map coordinates, without extreme signed-overflow claims.",
    "All direct Native callees now have canonical C owners. Actual world/pools/tables/routing/render/monument providers remain required; no IL or replacement callback.",
    "Existing child qualifications and genuine checked IDIV-fault status propagation remain. Native root logical return is void, not an EAX equivalence claim."
  ],
